  "question": {
    "text": "In a geometric progression consisting of positive terms, each term equals the sum of the next two terms. Then the common ratio of this progression equals"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\sqrt{5})$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{5}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{5}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{5}-1)$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $a r^{n-1}=a r^n+a r^{n+1}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow 1=r+r^2 \\\\\n& \\therefore r=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-1}{2} .\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}